        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Makapan-vallei': The established Afrikaans name is usually written 'Makapansvallei' (as in Makapansgat); it is a place name, appears twice, and was not changed here, so a person or the writer should confirm the intended spelling.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): ''n Wêrelderfenisterrein wat op die lys is vir mense se verlede daar. /': The decided-definition note for 'gemengde wêrelderfenisterrein' says 'mense se verlede' is too narrow because the ǂKhomani site is listed for the ǂKhomani-San's living culture, yet this lesson defines a cultural site by 'mense se verlede' and puts the ǂKhomani site in that list; fixing it needs a content decision, not a language edit."
